WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.750
The anchor is only half the system.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.475
The other half is the rode, everything between the anchor and the boat.

3
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:09.550
Look at the diagram.

4
00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.400
Most small boats use a length of chain at the anchor, then nylon line.

5
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:19.800
The chain keeps the pull low, along the bottom, and stands up to rocks and shells.

6
00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:23.125
The nylon stretches and absorbs the shock.

7
00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:26.400
Now the word that matters most: scope.

8
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:31.950
It’s the ratio of the rode you let out, to the distance from your bow down to the bottom.

9
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.275
Not just the water depth.

10
00:00:34.525 --> 00:00:37.825
The depth, plus the height of your bow above the water.

11
00:00:38.075 --> 00:00:40.350
Five to one is the minimum.

12
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:43.850
Seven to one is better, and more in heavy weather.

13
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.775
So try one.

14
00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:49.575
Fifteen feet of water, and your bow is three feet up.

15
00:00:49.825 --> 00:00:52.200
How much rode for seven to one?

16
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.600
Eighteen feet, times seven.

17
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:58.075
One hundred twenty-six feet.
